.Dd November 7, 2026
.Dt MOUNT_LITTLEFS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mount_littlefs
.Nd mount a littlefs file system with BSD metadata
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl b Ar block-size
.Op Fl o Ar options
.Ar special node
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
attaches the littlefs file system on the block device
.Ar special
to the directory
.Ar node .
The image must contain the BSD metadata attributes produced by
.Xr makefs 8
with the
.Fl t Cm littlefs
option.
Images without ownership and permission metadata are rejected.
.Pp
The
.Fl b
option specifies the erase block size for a regular block device.
The default is 4096 bytes.
For a NOR flash device the driver supplies the erase geometry.
The size must match the image and be a power of two.
.Pp
The
.Fl o
option accepts the standard
.Xr mount 8
options, including
.Cm ro , rw , update , noexec , nosuid , nodev ,
and
.Cm noatime .
The file system supports regular files, directories, symbolic links, device
nodes, FIFOs, Unix sockets, file permissions and ownership.
Hard links, NFS file handles, extended attributes exposed through the BSD
system calls, and access control lists are not supported.
.Pp
The root directory name
.Pa .littlefs-tmp
is reserved for interrupted file creation and is not exposed to applications.
Incomplete creates are removed when the file system is mounted read-write.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr makefs 8 ,
.Xr mount 8 ,
.Xr mount_tmpfs 8
